 "notes": [
  "Object table \"Standard BACnet objects\" and \"Description of values\", guide LE10699AF pages 229-235.",
  "Circuit groups are printed as instance ranges with one name; only the first object of each range is listed, the range is in the description (e.g. lighting BV 4-11, DALI groups AV 53-68 / BV 64-79).",
  "BUS SCS objects are numbered in the order peripherals were declared during configuration.",
  "The BUS SCS roller shutter/curtain object has no instance in the table and is marked \"under construction\"; it is left out.",
  "The text calls the ambient temperature objects Analog Values (0); type code 0 and the table say Analog Input.",
  "Scenario BOs are listed as write-only; a change of value 0->1 or 1->0 launches the scenario. Up to 128 simultaneous COV subscriptions."
